1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,190
Part nine. GST invoices and payments.

2
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:08,250
On the quotation, tap Convert to invoice.

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:13,478
The invoice is made with the same lines and the order is confirmed.

4
00:00:13,478 --> 00:00:16,522
It starts as a Draft, without a number.

5
00:00:17,410 --> 00:00:19,778
A draft can still be changed.

6
00:00:19,778 --> 00:00:24,023
When you send it to the customer, tap Issue invoice.

7
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:30,228
It gets the next number in the series, so cancelled drafts never leave gaps.

8
00:00:30,228 --> 00:00:35,290
After that, its lines and price are locked, as GST rules need.

9
00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:37,131
Print it.

10
00:00:37,131 --> 00:00:41,938
The tax invoice has your GSTIN, the customer's,

11
00:00:41,938 --> 00:00:49,508
the place of supply with its state code, HSN codes, CGST and SGST or IGST,

12
00:00:49,508 --> 00:00:56,361
the HSN summary, amount in words and a UPI QR code for the balance.

13
00:00:57,250 --> 00:01:00,599
When money comes in, tap Record payment.

14
00:01:00,599 --> 00:01:05,205
The balance is filled in; change it for a part payment.

15
00:01:05,205 --> 00:01:10,480
Choose how it was paid, add the UTR or cheque number, and save.

16
00:01:11,370 --> 00:01:14,124
The receipt is ready to print or send.

17
00:01:14,124 --> 00:01:18,255
The invoice now shows Partially Paid and the balance due.

18
00:01:18,255 --> 00:01:21,081
When everything is paid, it shows Paid.

19
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:28,460
For an overdue invoice, the WhatsApp button suggests a polite payment reminder with

20
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:31,666
the amount, the due date and your UPI ID.

21
00:01:31,666 --> 00:01:34,715
Overdue invoices also appear in alerts.

22
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:38,547
Next video: Projects and tasks.

